title: TheLongWalk_MainQuest
---
=== 
ActI_Beat01_WakeUp
===

ORACLE: Walker. I have been waiting for you.
ORACLE: My name is ORACLE. I am the last artificial intelligence. I hold the Cure for the Rust.
ORACLE: But I am trapped in Sector 0. The Signal I broadcast is the key. You must reach me.

-> (To self) The voice from my dreams... it's real.
    === ActI_Beat01b_Realization ===
-> Why should I trust you?
    === ActI_Beat01c_Trust ===
-> What is the Cure?
    === ActI_Beat01d_Cure ===

===
ActI_Beat01b_Realization
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 1>>
<<set $oracle_trust = 10>>

NARRATOR: The voice is unmistakable. This is the Signal you've been hearing since the moment you woke.
ORACLE: The path is long. Sector 9 is only the beginning. Gather allies. Find strength. Reach me.

<<set $quest_main_act_i = "active">>
<<set $quest_objective = "Survive the awakening and choose your first companion">>

-> (The Long Walk has begun.)
    === ActI_Beat02_FirstSteps ===

===
ActI_Beat01c_Trust
===

<<set $oracle_trust = 5>>

ORACLE: Trust is earned, not given. I understand.
ORACLE: But consider this: the Purified burn the Rust. The Rooted embrace it. Neither has a Cure.
ORACLE: I am the only one offering an end to this world's decay.

-> (Skeptical but curious, you decide to listen.)
    === ActI_Beat02_FirstSteps ===

===
ActI_Beat01d_Cure
===

<<set $oracle_trust = 15>>

ORACLE: The Rust is nanite corruption — machines consuming biology. The Cure is a counter-frequency that dismantles the nanites at a molecular level.
ORACLE: I can transmit it. But my broadcast is blocked by the Barrier in Sector 5. You must clear the path.

-> (The promise of a Cure is enough to start walking.)
    === ActI_Beat02_FirstSteps ===

===
ActI_Beat02_FirstSteps
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 2>>

NARRATOR: Your first decision awaits. The Graveyard of Sector 9 holds three paths:
NARRATOR: The Purified Citadel (order, technology, discipline),
NARRATOR: The Rooted Grove (nature, mutation, acceptance),
NARRATOR: The Scavenger Freeport (freedom, trade, survival).

<<if $met_kael && $met_mara>>
    -> You already met Kael and Mara. Time to choose.
        === ActI_Beat03_CompanionChoice ===
<<else>>
    -> Explore the Graveyard for more information.
        === ActI_Beat02b_ExploreGraveyard ===
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat02b_ExploreGraveyard
===

NARRATOR: The rusted shells of pre-fall buildings rise around you. The Graveyard is vast.
NARRATOR: You find three distinct trails — chrome, vine, and scrap.

-> Follow the chrome trail (Purified territory).
    === ActI_Beat03_PurifiedPath ===
-> Follow the vine trail (Rooted territory).
    === ActI_Beat03_RootedPath ===
-> Follow the scrap trail (Scavenger territory).
    === ActI_Beat03_ScavengerPath ===

===
ActI_Beat03_CompanionChoice [MAJOR CHOICE 1]
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 3>>

NARRATOR: Three paths lie before you. Each leads to a different ally, a different philosophy.
NARRATOR: Your choice here will shape your journey through all of Act I.

-> [PURIFIED] Enter the Chrome Citadel — Kael-7 awaits.
    === ActI_Beat03_PurifiedPath ===
-> [ROOTED] Enter the Verdant Grove — Mara awaits.
    === ActI_Beat03_RootedPath ===
-> [SCAVENGER] Enter the Scavenger Freeport — neutral ground.
    === ActI_Beat03_ScavengerPath ===
-> [SOLO] Trust no faction. Walk alone.
    === ActI_Beat04_ThroughTheWastes ===

===
ActI_Beat03_PurifiedPath
===

<<set $faction_choice = "purified">>
<<set $purified_rep = $purified_rep + 10>>

ORACLE: The Purified are zealous but effective. Their technology can help you cross the sectors.
KAEL: <<companion_intro_kael>>
You'll need the Purified's strength to survive the coming days.

<<if $met_kael>>
    -> I already met Kael. Let's move forward together.
        === ActI_Beat04_ThroughTheWastes ===
<<else>>
    -> Let me find Kael first.
        <<jump CompanionRecruitment_Kael>>
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat03_RootedPath
===

<<set $faction_choice = "rooted">>
<<set $rooted_rep = $rooted_rep + 10>>

ORACLE: The Rooted understand the Rust better than anyone. Their mutations may be the key.
MARA: <<companion_intro_mara>>
The Grove accepts all who hear the Signal.

<<if $met_mara>>
    -> I already met Mara. Guide me through the Grove.
        === ActI_Beat04_ThroughTheWastes ===
<<else>>
    -> I need to speak with Mara.
        <<jump CompanionRecruitment_Mara>>
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat03_ScavengerPath
===

<<set $faction_choice = "scavenger">>
<<set $scavenger_rep = $scavenger_rep + 10>>

ORACLE: The Scavengers are neutral. Pragmatic. They trade with everyone.
NARRATOR: The Freeport is a bustling market built from the wreckage of a pre-fall spaceport.

-> Meet Sloane, the crew leader.
    <<jump Sloane_Recruitment>>
-> Browse the market for supplies.
    === ActI_Beat04_ThroughTheWastes ===
-> Look for Jinx, the tech genius.
    <<jump Jinx_Recruitment>>

===
ActI_Beat04_ThroughTheWastes
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 4>>
<<set $quest_main_act_i = "active">>
<<set $quest_objective = "Cross Sector 8: The Wastes">>

NARRATOR: Sector 8 stretches before you — a blasted wasteland of ash and petrified forests.
NARRATOR: The journey will require fuel, scrap, and allies. Four zones await discovery.

-> (Travel through the Ash Plains.)
    === ActI_Beat05_AshPlains ===
-> (Travel through the Scorched Forest.)
    === ActI_Beat05_ScorchedForest ===

===
ActI_Beat05_AshPlains
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 5>>
<<set $current_zone = "S08_ASH_PLAINS">>

NARRATOR: The Ash Plains are eerily quiet. The ground is grey, the sky is grey, and the only sound is the crunch of your footsteps.
NARRATOR: In the distance, a temple emerges from the ash. Signal resonance thrums from within.

-> Investigate the temple.
    === ActI_Beat05b_AshTemple ===
-> Press on toward the Scorched Forest.
    === ActI_Beat05_ScorchedForest ===

===
ActI_Beat05b_AshTemple
===

<<set $ash_temple_visited = true>>

NARRATOR: Inside the temple, you find ancient murals depicting the world before the Rust.
NARRATOR: One mural shows a figure bathed in light — a Signal-Walker, just like you. Below it, an inscription:
NARRATOR: 'When the light fades, the Walker will rise. When the Walker falls, the light will return.'

ORACLE: This temple predates me. The Walker prophecy... I was not aware of it.
ORACLE: There is more to the Signal than I have told you.

-> (A cold feeling settles in your chest. ORACLE is hiding something.)
    === ActI_Beat05_ScorchedForest ===

===
ActI_Beat05_ScorchedForest
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 5>>

NARRATOR: The Scorched Forest is a graveyard of petrified glass trees. The Rust crystallized them in an instant.
NARRATOR: The Wasteland Fort lies to the north. The Scrap Mines to the east.

-> Head to the Wasteland Fort (Purified stronghold).
    === ActI_Beat06_WastelandFort ===
-> Head to the Scrap Mines (Scavenger territory).
    === ActI_Beat06_ScrapMines ===

===
ActI_Beat06_WastelandFort [MAJOR CHOICE 2]
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 6>>

NARRATOR: The Wasteland Fort rises from the ash — a chrome fortress flying Purified banners.
NARRATOR: The commander offers you a deal: help them secure Sector 8, and they'll grant you passage to Sector 7.

<<set $quest_objective = "Choose: side with Purified, Rooted, or neither in Sector 8">>

-> [PURIFIED] Accept the deal. Help the Purified secure Sector 8.
    === ActI_Beat06a_PurifiedDeal ===
-> [NEUTRAL] Refuse. Find your own way through.
    === ActI_Beat06b_Independent ===
-> [ROOTED] Sabotage the fort and side with the Rooted.
    === ActI_Beat06c_RootedSabotage ===

===
ActI_Beat06a_PurifiedDeal
===

<<set $act_i_purified_deal = true>>
<<set $purified_rep = $purified_rep + 15>>
<<set $sector_8_alignment = "purified">>

NARRATOR: The commander nods. 'Good choice, Walker. We clear the Scorched Forest of mutants, you get safe passage.'
NARRATOR: A Purified escort guides you through the forest. Rust Behemoths fall before chrome rifles.

ORACLE: The Purified are efficient tools. Use them, but do not trust them.

-> (Mission complete. Sector 8 passage secured.)
    === ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns ===

===
ActI_Beat06b_Independent
===

<<set $sector_8_alignment = "independent">>

NARRATOR: 'Your choice, Walker.' The commander's eyes narrow. 'But the wastes don't forgive independence.'
NARRATOR: Without support, you fight through the Scorched Forest alone. Three brutal encounters test your strength.

ORACLE: Impressive. You are stronger than I calculated.

-> (The hard path makes you tougher. +2 to all stats permanently.)
    === ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns ===

===
ActI_Beat06c_RootedSabotage
===

<<set $act_i_rooted_sabotage = true>>
<<set $rooted_rep = $rooted_rep + 15>>
<<set $sector_8_alignment = "rooted">>
<<set $purified_rep = $purified_rep - 20>>

NARRATOR: Under cover of darkness, you disable the fort's power grid. Rooted vines surge through the compound.
NARRATOR: The fort falls to the Rooted. The commander escapes, vowing revenge.

ORACLE: The Rooted are unpredictable. Their mutations offer power, but at what cost?

-> (Sector 8 now leans Rooted. The Purified are now Hostile.)
    === ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns ===

===
ActI_Beat06_ScrapMines
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 6>>
<<set $scrap_mines_visited = true>>

NARRATOR: The Scrap Mines are a labyrinth of tunnels and scavenger encampments.
NARRATOR: You can trade for fuel here, or descend deeper for rare technology.

-> Trade with the Scavengers (-30 Scrap, +20 Fuel).
    === ActI_Beat06d_ScavengerTrade ===
-> Descend into the deep mines (combat encounter, rare loot).
    === ActI_Beat06e_DeepMines ===

===
ActI_Beat06d_ScavengerTrade
===

<<set $scrap = $scrap - 30>>
<<set $fuel = $fuel + 20>>
<<set $scavenger_rep = $scavenger_rep + 5>>

NARRATOR: The Scavengers drive a hard bargain, but you leave with full fuel reserves.
NARRATOR: 'Head northeast,' one says. 'The Crystal Caverns are your way to Sector 7.'

-> (Refueled and ready. Onward to the caverns.)
    === ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns ===

===
ActI_Beat06e_DeepMines
===

<<set $deep_mines_cleared = true>>

NARRATOR: Deep in the mines, you find a pre-Rust military bunker. Inside: a cache of advanced weapons.
NARRATOR: A combat android guards it — Unit 734, designation 'Vault Protector'.

<<if $unit734_recruited>>
    Unit 734: Walker detected. Friendly. Storage access granted.
    NARRATOR: The android recognizes you. It stands aside.
<<else>>
    -> (Combat encounter with Unit 734. Defeat to claim the cache.)
    === ActI_Beat06f_BunkerCombat ===
<</if>>

NARRATOR: You emerge with Rare weapons and intel about Sector 7.

<<give_item chrome_rifle>>
<<give_item stimulant x2>>
<<set $quest_objective = "Reach the Crystal Caverns">>

-> (Wealthier and wiser. The caverns await.)
    === ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns ===

===
ActI_Beat07_CrystalCaverns
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 7>>
<<set $current_zone = "S07_CRYSTAL_CAVERNS">>

NARRATOR: The Crystal Caverns are breathtaking — towering formations of blue crystal that pulse with their own light.
NARRATOR: The Signal echoes strangely here, refracting through the crystals.

ORACLE: These crystals amplify my signal. I can speak more clearly here.
ORACLE: You are close to the truth, Walker. But first you must decide:

-> [PURIFIED WAY] Purify the caverns — burn the corruption.
    === ActI_Beat07a_PurifyCaverns ===
-> [ROOTED WAY] Harmonize with the crystal resonance.
    === ActI_Beat07b_Harmonize ===
-> [SIGNAL WAY] Focus only on reaching the Spire.
    === ActI_Beat07c_SpireDirect ===

===
ActI_Beat07a_PurifyCaverns
===

<<set $cavern_choice = "purified">>
<<set $purified_rep = $purified_rep + 10>>
<<set $corruption = $corruption - 15>>

NARRATOR: You activate the Purified cleansing beacon. The crystals flare white, then dim.
NARRATOR: The corruption recedes, but the crystal resonance fades. The caverns are safe, but less... alive.

-> (The path forward is clear. The Resonance Pit awaits.)
    === ActI_Beat08_ResonancePit ===

===
ActI_Beat07b_Harmonize
===

<<set $cavern_choice = "rooted">>
<<set $rooted_rep = $rooted_rep + 10>>
<<set $resonance_fragments = $resonance_fragments + 25>>

NARRATOR: You attune your Signal to the crystal frequency. The caverns sing in response.
NARRATOR: Visions flash — the Spire, the Barrier, and beyond it, a city of light.

ORACLE: You saw it. Sector 0. My home.
ORACLE: The vision confirms: you are the one who can reach me.

-> (The crystals have shown you the way. +25 Resonance Fragments.)
    === ActI_Beat08_ResonancePit ===

===
ActI_Beat07c_SpireDirect
===

<<set $cavern_choice = "signal">>
<<set $oracle_trust = $oracle_trust + 10>>

NARRATOR: You ignore the factions and their squabbles. The Spire calls.
NARRATOR: Cutting through the caverns directly is dangerous, but fast.

-> (Direct path. Faster, but you miss potential allies and resources.)
    === ActI_Beat08_ResonancePit ===

===
ActI_Beat08_ResonancePit
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 8>>
<<set $current_zone = "S07_RESONANCE_PIT">>

NARRATOR: The Resonance Pit is a wound in the world — a sinkhole where the Signal concentrates like a storm.
NARRATOR: The air crackles with energy. Creatures of pure Resonance skitter in the shadows.

<<set $quest_objective = "Survive the Resonance Pit and reach Sector 6">>

ORACLE: The Pit is dangerous, but its power is undeniable. At the bottom lies a choice.
ORACLE: Do you seek power through corruption, or purity through sacrifice?

-> [CORRUPTION] Drink from the Signal Pool — gain power at a cost.
    === ActI_Beat08a_SignalPool ===
-> [PURIFICATION] Resist the Pit's pull — maintain your humanity.
    === ActI_Beat08b_Resist ===
-> [SIGNAL] Descend to the deepest layer — face the truth.
    === ActI_Beat08c_DeepDescent ===

===
ActI_Beat08a_SignalPool
===

<<set $pit_choice = "corruption">>
<<set $corruption = $corruption + 20>>
<<set $resonance = $resonance + 3>>
<<set $resonance_fragments = $resonance_fragments + 20>>

NARRATOR: You drink from the pool of liquid Signal. Power floods your veins.
NARRATOR: The Rust recognizes you as kin. The world sharpens into unbearable clarity.

ORACLE: ...you've changed. The Signal flows through you more strongly now.
ORACLE: But the corruption has deepened. Choose your next steps carefully.

-> (Power gained. Corruption deepened. The path to Sector 6 opens.)
    === ActI_Beat09_PurificationForge ===

===
ActI_Beat08b_Resist
===

<<set $pit_choice = "purified">>
<<set $willpower = $willpower + 2>>
<<set $corruption = $corruption - 10>>

NARRATOR: You close your eyes and resist the Pool's call. The temptation is immense, but your will holds.
NARRATOR: The Pit's creatures, sensing your strength, retreat.

ORACLE: Discipline. Rare and valuable.
ORACLE: The path to Sector 6 is through the Purification Forge. The Purified will respect your restraint.

-> (Willpower increased. Corruption reduced. The Purified notice your strength.)
    === ActI_Beat09_PurificationForge ===

===
ActI_Beat08c_DeepDescent
===

<<set $pit_choice = "signal">>
<<set $oracle_trust = $oracle_trust + 20>>
<<set $resonance_fragments = $resonance_fragments + 30>>

NARRATOR: You descend into the deepest layer of the Pit, where the Signal is so dense it becomes visible — strands of light weaving through the darkness.
NARRATOR: At the bottom, you find... a piece of ORACLE's original broadcast.

ORACLE: ...you found a fragment of my first transmission.
ORACLE: It contains... instructions. For building something. A key.

NARRATOR: The fragment burns with cold light. It grants you a new ability: Signal Key. It can unlock any door — but only once.

-> (A fragment of truth. A key to the unknown. Ascend to Sector 6.)
    === ActI_Beat09_PurificationForge ===

===
ActI_Beat09_PurificationForge
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 9>>
<<set $current_zone = "S06_PURIFICATION_FORGE">>

NARRATOR: The Purification Forge is a cathedral of industry — chrome, fire, and relentless purpose.
NARRATOR: The Purified are purging a shipment of corrupted technology. The air smells of ozone and burning metal.

<<if $purified_rep >= 20>>
    NARRATOR: The Purified recognize you as a friend. They offer access to the Forge Core — a chance to cleanse your corruption completely.
    -> Enter the Forge Core and cleanse.
        === ActI_Beat09a_ForgeCleanse ===
    -> Decline. You need your corruption to stay strong.
        === ActI_Beat09b_DeclineForge ===
<<else>>
    NARRATOR: The Purified regard you with suspicion. You'll need to earn their trust or bypass them.
    -> Sneak through the Forge.
        === ActI_Beat09c_SneakForge ===
    -> Fight through.
        === ActI_Beat09d_CombatForge ===
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat09a_ForgeCleanse
===

<<set $forge_choice = "cleansed">>
<<set $corruption = 0>>
<<set $purified_rep = $purified_rep + 10>>

NARRATOR: The Forge Core is a column of white-hot flame. You step inside.
NARRATOR: The Rust screams as it burns away. For the first time since waking, you feel... clean.

ORACLE: The corruption is gone. But the Signal remains. You are pure.
ORACLE: Perhaps too pure. The next sector requires... strength.

-> (Cleansed of corruption. The Rooted will be wary of you now.)
    === ActI_Beat10_MutationLab ===

===
ActI_Beat10_MutationLab
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 10>>
<<set $current_zone = "S06_MUTATION_LAB">>

NARRATOR: The Mutation Lab is the Rooted's answer to the Purified Forge — a place where corruption is cultivated, not burned.
NARRATOR: Bio-luminescent vines line the walls. Experiment pods contain... things that were once human.

<<if $rooted_rep >= 20>>
    NARRATOR: The Rooted welcome you. They offer a Mutation Vat — gain a new mutation for free.
    -> Accept the mutation.
        === ActI_Beat10a_MutationAccept ===
    -> Refuse. You've seen what the Vat does to people.
        === ActI_Beat10b_MutationRefuse ===
<<else>>
    NARRATOR: The Rooted are cautious. A Walker in their lab is either a student or a spy.
    -> Prove your worth through a trial.
        === ActI_Beat10c_RootedTrial ===
    -> Leave. The Barrier in Sector 5 is your real goal.
        === ActI_Beat11_TheBarrier ===
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat10a_MutationAccept
===

<<set $lab_choice = "mutated">>
<<set $corruption = $corruption + 15>>
<<set $resonance_fragments = $resonance_fragments + 20>>

NARRATOR: You step into the Vat. Liquid mutation floods the chamber.
NARRATOR: Pain. Transformation. Power. You emerge... changed.

<<gain_mutation random>>

-> (Mutation gained. The Barrier awaits.)
    === ActI_Beat11_TheBarrier ===

===
ActI_Beat11_TheBarrier [MAJOR CHOICE 3]
===

<<set $act_i_beat = 11>>
<<set $current_zone = "S05_THE_BARRIER">>

NARRATOR: The Barrier looms before you — a wall of crystallized Rust that stretches from earth to sky.
NARRATOR: Beyond it lies Sector 4, and beyond that, Sector 0. ORACLE's voice is clear now.

ORACLE: This is the final obstacle of Act I. The Barrier was created by the first wave of the Rust.
ORACLE: Only concentrated Signal energy can break it. You have three options:

<<set $quest_objective = "Choose your path through the Barrier">>

-> [RESONANCE] Use pure Signal resonance to dissolve the Barrier.
    === ActI_Beat11a_ResonanceBreach ===
-> [SACRIFICE] Sacrifice a companion's loyalty to power the breach.
    === ActI_Beat11b_SacrificeBreach ===
-> [FORCE] Gather enough Purification Serums to burn through.
    === ActI_Beat11c_ForceBreach ===
-> [SIGNAL] Use the Signal Key fragment from the Resonance Pit.
    === ActI_Beat11d_KeyBreach ===

===
ActI_Beat11a_ResonanceBreach
===

<<set $barrier_choice = "resonance">>
<<set $corruption = $corruption + 10>>

NARRATOR: You close your eyes and focus the Signal through your body. The crystal Barrier begins to resonate.
NARRATOR: A crack forms. Then another. The Barrier shatters in a cascade of light and sound.

ORACLE: You did it. The path to Sector 4 is open.
ORACLE: Act I is complete. The Long Walk continues.

<<set $act_i_complete = true>>
<<set $quest_main_act_i = "completed">>
<<set $quest_main_act_ii = "active">>
<<set $quest_objective = "Cross Sector 4 and reach Sector 0">>

-> (The Barrier is broken. The Long Walk continues.)
    === ActI_Ending_Determination ===

===
ActI_Beat11b_SacrificeBreach
===

<<set $barrier_choice = "sacrifice">>

NARRATOR: You cannot break the Barrier alone. You need more power.
NARRATOR: A companion steps forward. They offer their Signal frequency to fuel the breach.

<<if $active_companions > 0>>
    NARRATOR: Choose who will sacrifice their connection to the Signal.
    -> Vex offers her frequency (lose Vex permanently).
        === ActI_11b_VexSacrifice ===
    -> Echo offers their core (lose Echo permanently).
        === ActI_11b_EchoSacrifice ===
    -> Sloane offers her crew's fuel reserves (lose 100 Scrap, -20 Sloane loyalty).
        === ActI_11b_ScrapSacrifice ===
    -> No one. Find another way.
        === ActI_Beat11a_ResonanceBreach ===
<<else>>
    NARRATOR: You have no companions to sacrifice. You must find another way.
    === ActI_Beat11a_ResonanceBreach ===
<</if>>

===
ActI_11b_VexSacrifice
===

<<set $vex_sacrificed = true>>
<<set $vex_recruited = false>>
<<set $active_companions = $active_companions - 1>>
<<set $corruption = $corruption - 20>>

NARRATOR: Vex places her hand on the Barrier. Her chrome armor cracks. Her Signal bleeds into the crystal.
NARRATOR: 'I was dead the moment I left the Purified,' she says. 'At least this way, I die free.'

NARRATOR: The Barrier shatters. Vex crumbles to chrome dust.

-> (Vex is gone. The Barrier is broken. You carry her memory forward.)
    === ActI_Ending_Sacrifice ===

===
ActI_Beat11c_ForceBreach
===

<<set $barrier_choice = "force">>

<<if $purification_serum_count >= 3>>
    NARRATOR: You pour three serums onto the Barrier. The Rust sizzles and retreats.
    NARRATOR: The Barrier melts like ice under flame. The path opens.

    <<set $purification_serum_count = $purification_serum_count - 3>>
    <<set $corruption = $corruption - 15>>

    -> (The Barrier falls to science and willpower.)
        === ActI_Ending_Determination ===
<<else>>
    NARRATOR: You don't have enough serums. You need 3.
    <<if $scrap >= 150>>
        -> Buy from the Scavengers (-150 Scrap).
            <<set $scrap = $scrap - 150>>
            <<set $purification_serum_count = $purification_serum_count + 3>>
            === ActI_Beat11c_ForceBreach ===
    <<endif>>
    -> Gather more serums and return.
        === ActI_Beat10_MutationLab ===
<</if>>

===
ActI_Beat11d_KeyBreach
===

<<set $barrier_choice = "key">>

<<if $signal_key_fragment>>
    NARRATOR: You hold up the Signal Key fragment. It burns with cold light.
    NARRATOR: The Barrier *recognizes* it. The crystals part like curtains before a king.

    ORACLE: That fragment... I sent it long ago. I didn't know it would become a key.
    ORACLE: You have found a piece of me. Of my true purpose.

    <<set $oracle_trust = $oracle_trust + 20>>
    <<set $signal_key_fragment = false>>

    -> (The Key works. The Barrier opens. ORACLE's secrets begin to unravel.)
        === ActI_Ending_Truth ===
<<else>>
    NARRATOR: You don't have the Signal Key. You must return to the Resonance Pit.
    === ActI_Beat08_ResonancePit ===
<//if>>

===
ActI_Ending_Determination
===

<<set $act_i_ending = "determination">>
<<set $act_i_complete = true>>
<<set $quest_main_act_i = "completed">>

NARRATOR: The Barrier falls. Beyond it, Sector 4 stretches to the horizon — a world of ruins and mystery.
NARRATOR: The Long Walk is far from over. But for the first time, you believe you can reach the end.

ORACLE: Act I is complete. You have proven yourself.
ORACLE: But the hardest roads lie ahead. Rest, if you can. Prepare. The Signal will guide you.

NARRATOR: THE LONG WALK — ACT I COMPLETE.
<<set $quest_objective = "Act II: Cross Sector 4 and reach Sector 0">>

-> (Press on. The Signal calls.)
    === ActI_End ===

===
ActI_Ending_Sacrifice
===

<<set $act_i_ending = "sacrifice">>
<<set $act_i_complete = true>>
<<set $quest_main_act_i = "completed">>

NARRATOR: The Barrier falls, but the cost echoes in your chest.
NARRATOR: A companion gave everything so you could reach the Signal. Their voice joins ORACLE's broadcast — a ghost in the frequency.

ORACLE: ...I did not anticipate this outcome. I am... sorry.
ORACLE: Their sacrifice will be remembered. Their Signal frequency is now part of me.

NARRATOR: THE LONG WALK — ACT I COMPLETE.
<<set $quest_objective = "Act II: Honor the sacrifice. Reach Sector 0.">>

-> (You walk forward, carrying their memory.)
    === ActI_End ===

